    "scope": {
      "id": "scope",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Game-owned knowledge storage, graph ingestion, textual search, structured graph queries, and the boundary between knowledge and callable GameCube decomp tools."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "ownership-heading": {
      "id": "ownership-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Ownership"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "ownership-body": {
      "id": "ownership-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Melee owns its source descriptors, generated evidence, graph database, tool bindings, and tool output under "
        },
        {
          "insert": "games/melee",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Reusable callable capabilities live under "
        },
        {
          "insert": "toolpacks/gamecube-decomp",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Server runtime code resolves those game resources and builds or queries the graph from "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "files-heading": {
      "id": "files-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "File Tree"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "files-tree": {
      "id": "files-tree",
      "type": "file-tree",
      "props": {
        "entries": [
          {
            "path": "games/melee/knowledge/sources/registry.json",
            "note": "active source catalog"
          },
          {
            "path": "games/melee/knowledge/sources/injectable/",
            "note": "compact injected standards"
          },
          {
            "path": "games/melee/knowledge/sources/rag_search/",
            "note": "directly searched corpora"
          },
          {
            "path": "games/melee/knowledge/sources/code_context/",
            "note": "code-connected source metadata and maintained corpora"
          },
          {
            "path": "games/melee/graph/graph.sqlite",
            "note": "materialized game graph"
          },
          {
            "path": "games/melee/shared/tool-data/",
            "note": "stable evidence generated by tool runners"
          },
          {
            "path": "games/melee/worktrees/<worktree_id>/tool-cache/",
            "note": "mutable worktree-local tool output"
          },
          {
            "path": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge/graph/builders/",
            "note": "source-specific record builders"
          },
          {
            "path": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge/graph/storage/",
            "note": "schema, ingest, search, and database access"
          },
          {
            "path": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge/graph/queries/",
            "note": "structured read models"
          },
          {
            "path": "toolpacks/gamecube-decomp/",
            "note": "tool definitions, APIs, runners, and shared implementations"
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "storage-heading": {
      "id": "storage-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Graph Storage"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "storage-body": {
      "id": "storage-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The active game graph is SQLite. Its Drizzle schema is defined in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge/graph/storage/schema.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Builders produce normalized records, and rebuild ingestion materializes a coherent graph rather than maintaining a separate database for each source."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "storage-records": {
      "id": "storage-records",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Core tables: source and tool descriptors, resource versions, entities, facts, edges, search chunks, worker updates, and merged-PR updates."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "build-heading": {
      "id": "build-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Build And Ingestion"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "build-body": {
      "id": "build-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Graph rebuild starts from registered descriptors, resets materialized graph records, runs the selected builders, and inserts their entities, facts, edges, and search chunks. The default builder set is defined in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge/graph/builders/rebuild.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "build-inputs": {
      "id": "build-inputs",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Default inputs cover the code graph, past PRs, standards, agent and curator evidence, mismatch patterns, opseq similarity, call-graph edges, siblings, and the knowledge ledger. Tool runners refresh binary-derived evidence before a maintenance rebuild."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "similarity-heading": {
      "id": "similarity-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Similarity And Relationships"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "similarity-body": {
      "id": "similarity-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Opseq computes function similarity outside the database from opcode fingerprints. Its builder stores the results as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "ANALOGOUS_TO",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " edges and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "opseq_analog_profile",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " facts. Call-graph extraction similarly becomes "
        },
        {
          "insert": "CALLS",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "REFERENCES_DATA",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " edges. The graph stores and connects computed evidence; it does not calculate a generic similarity metric at query time."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "search-heading": {
      "id": "search-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Text Search"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "search-body": {
      "id": "search-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Graph text search queries "
        },
        {
          "insert": "search_chunks",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with SQLite FTS5 when available and a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "LIKE",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " fallback. Results are ranked from literal query and term matches in titles and text. The implementation is in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge/graph/storage/search.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "search-boundary": {
      "id": "search-boundary",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Text search is lexical. It does not use embeddings, vector indexes, or automatic edge traversal. A caller may search all chunks or constrain results to one source id."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "queries-heading": {
      "id": "queries-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Structured Queries"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "queries-body": {
      "id": "queries-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Relationship-aware reads use dedicated query modules rather than text search. File cards combine editability, match status, PR history, source-linked chunks, mismatch patterns, opseq analogs, and scheduling signals. Rank-feature queries expose graph evidence used by scheduling. Additional edge types require an explicit query surface before agents can consume them reliably."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "tools-heading": {
      "id": "tools-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Tool Boundary"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "tools-body": {
      "id": "tools-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A tool is a callable operation, not a parallel knowledge store. Research runners such as opseq, callgraph, and Ghidra produce evidence that graph builders can ingest. Validation, compiler, source-editing, and data-conversion tools remain direct actions because their purpose is to inspect or transform a concrete attempt. Stable outputs live under game shared tool data; mutable outputs remain worktree-local."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-heading": {
      "id": "maintenance-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Maintenance"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-body": {
      "id": "maintenance-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Knowledge maintenance refreshes generated evidence and rebuilds the game graph. Individual graph jobs support inspection and targeted refreshes."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
